# Implementation Plan: Production-Ready Scalability for 1 Million Users

This plan details the technical roadmap to restructure and optimize the CareSync (iCare) platform to handle 1 million users with high performance, security, and reliability.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Database Scaling**
> 1 million users requires more than just indexing; we should prepare for **Read Replicas** in the database layer. I will restructure the database client to support a primary-replica model.

> [!CAUTION]
> **Infrastructure Requirements**
> To support this scale, we will need:
> 1. **Redis**: For caching and session management.
> 2. **Sentry/Axiom**: For centralized error tracking and logging.
> 3. **Rate Limiting**: Integrated via Upstash or a similar edge-optimized service.

## Proposed Changes

### Database Layer (`packages/db`)

#### [MODIFY] [schema.ts](file:///d:/Projects/caresync/packages/db/src/schema.ts)
- Add indexing to all high-frequency query columns:
    - `usersTable`: `email`, `role`.
    - `patientsTable`: `userId`.
    - `hospitalsTable`: `userId`, `approvalStatus`.
    - `doctorsTable`: `hospitalId`, `userId`, `isAvailable`.
    - `appointmentsTable`: `patientId`, `hospitalId`, `doctorId`, `status`, `appointmentDate`.
    - `medicalRecordsTable`: `patientId`, `hospitalId`, `recordDate`.

#### [MODIFY] [index.ts](file:///d:/Projects/caresync/packages/db/src/index.ts)
- Optimize connection pooling:
    - Increase `connectionLimit`.
    - Adjust `idleTimeout` and `maxIdle`.
- Support for **Read Replicas** to offload heavy `SELECT` queries from the writer node.

---

### Authentication & Security (`packages/core/auth`)

#### [MODIFY] [auth.ts](file:///d:/Projects/caresync/apps/admin/src/lib/auth.ts) & similar
- **Refresh Tokens**: Implement short-lived access tokens (15m) and long-lived refresh tokens (7d) stored in secure, `httpOnly` cookies.
- **CSRF Protection**: Implement a synchronizer token pattern or generic double-submit cookies.

